Palm verification runs on the citizen's own device and on SOV Network nodes.
No biometric image, template or embedding is transmitted to any platform that
uses SOV for identity.

THIRD-PARTY MODELS
------------------
This application ships three TensorFlow Lite models as assets. They run entirely on
the citizen's device and transmit nothing. They are binary files, so their provenance
cannot be read out of them -- it is recorded in THIRD_PARTY_MODELS.md, which every
redistributor should read:

  assets/models/blazeface_short.tflite
      Google MediaPipe BlazeFace (short range), unmodified. Apache-2.0, the same
      licence as this project.

  assets/models/svrn_model.tflite
      SOV's own palm detector, trained on public data (11k Hands + COCO negatives).
      The training script is published at tools/training/svrn_v28_retrain.py.
      It fine-tunes from Ultralytics' pretrained yolov8n.pt, and Ultralytics assert
      that models produced with their software are subject to AGPL-3.0. That claim
      is contested and unsettled; THIRD_PARTY_MODELS.md states both sides and does
      not pretend the question is closed. SOV publishes the complete corresponding
      source either way.

  assets/models/mobilefacenet.tflite
      A pretrained MobileFaceNet face-embedding model. Its exact upstream source and
      licence are NOT recorded by this project -- an open gap, stated rather than
      guessed at.

SOV's own source remains under the Apache License 2.0 (see LICENSE, and
docs/LICENSING_DECISION_20260801.md for why).
